Z||000000||jhar||09-19-1999||07:27 PM||||my 87 has idle trouble ulike any i have read about. when you start the car the idle goes to 1500 then down to 600 and bounces to 1200. i show no codes. i have changed all vac.lines,all tbi sensers,the tbi itself,the o2 senser, and i even cut the exhaust loose. nothing has helped.as the car gets warmer it seems to be better but still idles bad at stop lites and usually dies.any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||09-19-1999||08:07 PM||||Have you checked the EGR valve to see if it was working or the tube that goes to it, which often cracks?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-20-1999||09:48 AM||||The EGR on the 4 cyl doen't have the infamous cracking tube. It's bolted directly to the intake.<P>A bad/loose EGR or any other vacuum leak would cause problems. Your problem is only at idle, but have you check fuel pressure just to make sure it's ok? <P>it's an 87 so it should be a DIS motor. did you replace the plugs and wires? You didn't put in platinum plugs did you?||||reg||1
Z||000003||jhar||09-20-1999||09:35 PM||||theogre i sent you an e-mail before i saw the post reply! i put platinums in,what did i screw up???||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-20-1999||11:49 PM||||I feel redundant........<P>platinum plugs such as the Bosch design burn out the center electrode when used in DIS motors. Autolite platinums, which are of a more traditional design, have not been tested yet as far as I know. If you have installed platinum plugs with the very fine Bosch type center electrode I would remove and replace them.<P>Replace them with either traditional style plugs or Accell U groove ones. Split fires have worked for me, but other people have had problems with the quality of this line.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||jhar||09-21-1999||05:51 PM||||thanks theogre for your input,were going to change plugs tonite...||||reg||6
Z||000006||jhar||09-21-1999||08:16 PM||||need an opinion from fellow fiero finatics. went out and started the 2.5,after she went through her 5min. of stalling and restarting she idled pretty good.BUT when i held the idle at 1800rpm she was shuttering and popping thur the exhaust.the tach would bounce around alittle, hmmm i think it might be time for a rebuild!! all those in favor say I!!!||||reg||8
